{"id": "1.2-00033", "case_id": "opencores_configurable_cordic_direct_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "opencores/arithmetic_core_configurable_cordic_core_in_verilog", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00033&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (6 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: cordic.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00033&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>1 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00033&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Fcordic.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed frozen testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>1 frozen testpoints:</strong> upstream91. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00033&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00033&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># First-quadrant CORDIC project\nImplement the complete three-module cordic project in cordic.v using the original manual.pdf in specification/. This is one integrated project even though the three modules share a file. The original manual supplies the micro-rotation algorithm, gain compensation, modes, numeric formats and implementation choices.\n\nCurator configuration and interface clarification:\n- Freeze the upstream default PIPELINE/ROTATE/RADIAN_16 configuration. Inputs/outputs x/y/theta are signed 17-bit values with 15 fractional bits; theta is in radians. The useful sine/cosine envelope is first-quadrant angles 0..pi/2 with x_i=19896 and y_i=0, compensating the CORDIC gain. Output x is cosine and y is sine, both scaled by 32768. No full-circle coarse rotation, VECTOR, iterative or combinational alternatives are required.\n- The original ITERATIONS define is 16, but the pinned pipeline generates fifteen rotator stages with indices 0..14. Preserve that fifteeen-stage registered configuration, receiving a new input each rising clk edge. rst is synchronous active-high and clears each rotator state; no valid or enable signals exist. After reset, discard pipeline fill outputs. Angles are quantized before application; at the original 91 integer-degree samples, each output must be within 10 integer LSB of the original fixed-point reference table.\n- Each rotator uses arithmetic right shifts by its iteration parameter, signed addition/subtraction and the corresponding quantized atan(2^-iteration), choosing direction from the residual angle sign. signed_shifter implements sign-extending right shift. The two body parameters of rotator (iteration and tangle) are included explicitly in interfaces/modules.v. Top exports the final residual theta without gain correction. Internal wires and state encodings are unrestricted.\n- The declaration and golden implementation are preprocessed from pinned default macros, with originals retained. The manual&#x27;s high-level stage count is clarified above; no executable algorithm has been changed. The private point retains all 91 upstream angle vectors, adding assertions for unknown results, exact vector count and the original 10-LSB tolerance. One entire testbench is one testpoint.\n\nImplement every required path in output_contract.json. Declaration-only ports\nare in interfaces/modules.v. No initial/final, delays, simulation system tasks,\nforce/release or external includes are permitted. Only declared RTL is collected.\nMissing files, forbidden constructs or failed top compilation score zero. Each\nprivate point has equal weight and requires all of its checks to pass. Use\nterminal/file_editor, iverilog, vvp and Python iteratively; finish by saving RTL.\nRun `python3 checks/check.py` for public compilation feedback.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/05f1d0f7f243f29213ddfcb8bce66f2df9384e7a7a57bc8cb902592e079a046b.txt", "size": 7577, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/771e58998dfa59d19bd4591ce49673fcbadd56239829b74d2a9c5869aef77295.txt", "size": 4693, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/cordic.v", "url": "assets/cac2938ca7774fc64239f9c1d6e7d36aab39717f2302b4cd81857c27faa3afbf.txt", "size": 12622, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_testbenches/tb_cordic.v", "url": "assets/3deac6b045a81939027563cec4ca8c033d07329273c46a62899ea903a3b521db.txt", "size": 9539, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/preprocessing/cordic/command.json", "url": "assets/a814383c3483edf1e22180ace7c4c15fdc2e469e089d236559969dd9bca96f06.txt", "size": 235, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/golden/project_compile.command.json", "url": "assets/0fa76433546b8730887573f1b18b576096d31ec8bd7a5bd47f2fcead1472330c.txt", "size": 2045, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/golden/project_compile.result.json", "url": "assets/1e3f6691f455051e8adb15d961e4bf3c7a17e83dd88b2afdd13315cc288250bb.txt", "size": 22, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and 